  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}$ is a $\\mathrm{d}^6$ ion. With strong field ligand like $\\mathrm{NH}_3,\\left[\\mathrm{Co}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_3\\right)_6\\right]^{3+}$ has no unpaired electron. For $\\mathrm{Co}^{3+}, \\mathrm{F}^{-}$is a weak field ligand.\n$\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}$ is a $\\mathrm{d}^6$ ion. With strong field ligand $\\mathrm{CN}^{-},\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{4-}$ has no unpaired electron. $\\mathrm{For}_{\\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}}, \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ is a weak field ligand.",
    "image": null
